change:
  id: CHG-009
  title: Invoke ACP agents through the harness boundary
  status: proposed
  intent: Add the first real external-agent adapter by invoking an ACP-compatible local subprocess over stdio while keeping routing, budgets, evidence and deterministic approval in SAAA.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - SYS-001
    - ARCH-001
    - ADR-0003
    - Q-010
    - Q-011

deltas:
  - op: ADDED
    capability: agent-harness-boundary
    requirement: SAAA can invoke a configured ACP agent subprocess over stdio, provide a bounded mutation request, capture streamed agent text and map a valid mutation envelope into AgentRunResult.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: an ACP agent subprocess is configured and the invocation budget is available
        then: SAAA initializes ACP, creates a session in the requested workspace, prompts the agent and parses one bounded mutation envelope
        and:
          - the ACP command and arguments are adapter configuration
          - the route remains caller-selected intent and the resulting mutation remains only a proposal
          - streamed output is retained as a digest, not as an unbounded result field
          - streamed output is bounded to 65536 characters before parsing or digesting
      - id: S2
        when: the ACP process fails, times out or returns malformed mutation text
        then: the harness returns FAILED or TIMED_OUT with no mutation and a bounded failure reason
      - id: S3
        when: the request has exhausted input, output or wall-clock allowance
        then: the harness returns REJECTED without starting the subprocess

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: adapters/acp/AcpAgentHarnessTest.parsesTheBoundedMutationEnvelopeFromAgentText
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: adapters/acp/AcpAgentHarnessTest.rejectsMalformedMutationEnvelope
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: adapters/acp/AcpAgentHarnessTest.recordsAFailedAcpSubprocessWithoutCreatingAMutation
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: adapters/acp/AcpAgentHarnessTest.refusesAnInvocationWhenTheBudgetIsExhausted
    layer: unit

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: add the official ACP Java SDK dependency and stdio adapter configuration
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: implement ACP initialize, session, prompt, streamed text capture and mutation mapping
    status: completed
  - id: T3
    slice: add bounded failure, timeout and budget tests and document the adapter
    status: completed
  - id: T4
    slice: exercise a real configured OpenCode, Goose, Codex or Claude ACP command in an opt-in environment
    status: pending

non_goals:
  - adding ACP, MCP or vendor types to domain or deterministic
  - selecting a provider or harness automatically
  - exposing raw agent output through AgentRunResult
  - changing deterministic validation, scoring or promotion

risks:
  - ACP protocol support and agent output semantics vary by implementation; opt-in real-agent coverage remains follow-up T4
  - ACP does not report provider billing usage in this adapter, so usage is currently measured only as wall-clock evidence
